      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "In plain words",
      "items": [
        "ARM64 code finds data with an ADRP + ADD pair",
        "ADRP counts from the start of a 4 KB page, so you need the load address mod 4 KB (the page phase)",
        "With the wrong phase, every string reference lands on a different string",
        "The disassembly still looks fine, so it fails silently"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "The numbers, and what it cost",
      "items": [
        "Phase 0: every reference lands exactly 0x800 bytes (2 KB) off; about 1,000 land on a clean string start",
        "Phase 0x800: about 4,249 land on a clean string start (tools/phase_test.py)",
        "0x12349876 is the identifier at the top of every Samsung PIT file; under phase 0 that check was written up as a Knox Guard token gate",
        "At the right phase the same check references guid_part.c (partition-table integrity)",
        "0x8f000000 is a ldr;br jump literal, the VA of file offset 0x61800"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Take-away",
      "items": [
        "Measure the phase instead of assuming zero",
        "Pin the load base too: the phase reads strings, the base makes the disassembler's own analysis work",
        "On a raw image an empty cross-reference list proves nothing",
        "Get a blind second pass: the first pass here invented a lock that was not there"
      ]
    }
  ]
